+# Run U (U1 to U3), 2026-11-10
+
+Scripted regression run of sub-slice U on a keyless server (port 3017, the builder's own), game
+128, headless Chromium through the `window.__test` bridge. Session log and captured responses were
+kept in the builder's scratchpad (`u-session.jsonl`, `u-responses.jsonl`). Nothing typed; no
+secret used.
+
+| Beat | Result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| U1 | **Pass** | Lena polled once a second: `goto_target:lena_pc`, `using:lena_pc` for 5 s, then `goto_target:kiosk_pc` with "USB's disabled. Typical." showing, `using:kiosk_pc`, `returning`, `idle`. The keyboard-type device went to `lena_pc` and was used there with no line. Tasks `u1_refused`, `u1_kiosk`, `u1_hid` completed |
+| U2 | **Pass** | Priya: `using:priya_pc`, then `idle` with "Blocked again. Brilliant."; the stick lay visible at (496, 107) in `vault_room`, and 15 s later she was still idle (not picked up again). Dock click: the alert "USB devices are disabled on this PC.", `vault_usb_2` still in the inventory, `u2_dock_planted` false. Tasks `u2_refused`, `u2_dock` completed |
+| U3 | **Pass** | Kofi: `goto_item`, `goto_target:lost_property_tray`, `using`, `idle`, with no line at any poll. Task `u3_tray` completed |
+
+`verify-run.rb 128 --access`: no sessions, sign-ins, clones, copies, failures or lockouts, as
+expected (sub-slice U writes nothing on the server).
+
+`access-leak-check.rb 128 u-responses.jsonl`: every rule 0, `VERDICT: no leaks found.`
+
+Harness note: the first `interact` on `vault_usb_2` from across the lobby landed on a neighbouring
+stick (`approach-click-acted`); a `moveToNear` then `interact` picked it up. A harness matter with
+five items a tile apart, not a game bug.
